      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An 80-year-old male patient presented with acute chest pain. Clinically an aortic dissection or pulmonary embolism was suspected therefore non-ECG-gated multislice computed tomography was performed and despite the lacking ECG gating the causative high grade coronary stenosis could be identified."},
